    -- A license configuration is an abstraction of a customer license agreement that can be
    -- consumed and enforced by License Manager. Components include specifications for the license
    -- type (licensing by instance, socket, CPU, or vCPU), allowed tenancy (shared tenancy,
    -- Dedicated Instance, Dedicated Host, or all of these), host affinity (how long a VM
    -- must be associated with a host), and the number of licenses purchased and used.
